  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering Women and Girls Affected by Migration and Forced Displacement in Honduras, Guatemala and El Salvador</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project focuses on the most urgent and high-impact requirements of the governments of El Salvador, Guatemala and Honduras to reduce the drivers of high-risk migration and forced displacement and facilitate return, reintegration or international protection to women and girls with an integrated humanitarian-development perspective. The main objective of the project is to contribute to improve well-being of women and girls in vulnerability affected by irregular migration and forced displacement in targeted areas of El Salvador, Guatemala and Honduras. The initiatives included in the project address the situation of vulnerable women and girls on the move and are aligned with the national priorities of the countries and the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development, the IOM Regional Strategy for Central America, North America and the Caribbean 2020-2024, the Comprehensive Regional Protection and Solutions Framework (MIRPS), and the state-led application of the Global Compact on Refugees and Global Compact for Migration in Central America.</narrative>
  </description>
